══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  MCP client configuration — paste this ONCE for all projects:

    {
      "mcpServers": {
        "dejafix": {
          "command": "/opt/djf/bin/djf-mcp",
          "args": []
        }
      }
    }

  You already have 2 other project(s) registered. The config
  above reaches all of them from one server.

  This project is registered as 'myproj'. Your AI can
  pass project="<name>" on any call, or you can set a default:
    djf project use myproj

  Codex uses TOML, not JSON — for ~/.codex/config.toml:

    [mcp_servers.dejafix]
    command = "/opt/djf/bin/djf-mcp"
    args = []

  Client config file locations:
    Claude Desktop  ~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json
    Cursor          ~/.cursor/mcp.json  (global; per-project is <repo>/.cursor/mcp.json)
    Antigravity     ~/.gemini/antigravity/mcp_config.json  (legacy IDE; v2 path may differ)
    Codex (TOML!)   ~/.codex/config.toml
    Claude Code     claude mcp add  (or ~/.claude.json)

  After pasting: fully quit and restart your client (cold start).
  Pinned to one repo instead:  djf init --mcp-config-single
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
